      "text": "Hack. Build. Innovate. Solve real-world problems. Maya Devi University presents Algonex 1.0 , an exciting hackathon where you turn ideas into working solutions. Whether you are a seasoned developer, a UI/UX enthusiast, an AI explorer, a problem solver, or someone with a great idea, this is the opportunity to build something meaningful, collaborate with like-minded innovators, and showcase your skills. What is Algonex 1.0? Algonex is a hands-on innovation challenge designed to encourage students to identify real-world problems and develop creative, technology-driven solutions. Participants will work in teams to ideate, design, develop, and present their solutions to a panel of judges. From AI and Web Development to Blockchain, IoT, Cybersecurity, Mobile Applications, and emerging technologies , participants are encouraged to think beyond conventional solutions and build something impactful. Why Participate? Build a real project from idea to implementation Put your coding, design, problem-solving and innovation skills to the test Work with teammates from diverse technical backgrounds Get an opportunity to showcase your project to industry/academic experts Compete with talented students and innovators Earn certificates, recognition and exciting prizes Add a meaningful project to your resume and portfolio Meet fellow developers, creators and future entrepreneurs Who Can Participate? The hackathon is open to students from all disciplines and departments . You don’t need to be an expert programmer. If you have an idea, a willingness to learn, and the drive to build, you belong here. Students interested in AI/ML, Web & App Development, Cybersecurity, Blockchain, IoT, Cloud, UI/UX, Data Science and other technology domains are encouraged to participate. The Challenge Identify. Ideate. Build. Pitch. Participants will be given the opportunity to work on meaningful problem statements and develop innovative solutions using technology. The focus isn’t just on writing code, it’s about solving problems. Think differently. Build boldly. Create something that matters. Event Highlights Ideation → Development → Testing → Presentation → Evaluation Participants will get a limited amount of time to transform their ideas into functional prototypes and pitch their solutions to the judging panel. Projects will be evaluated on factors such as: Innovation & Originality Problem Relevance Technical Implementation Creativity & Design Feasibility & Scalability Impact Presentation & Pitch Ready to test your skills? Bring your ideas, laptop, skills, creativity and a lot of enthusiasm . The mountains may be high, but the possibilities are higher. Build something. Break boundaries.",
